<title>SWITZERLAND: Hong Kong 2nd busiest cargo airport in April - ACI.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong 2nd busiest cargo airport in April - ACI.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong climbed to second place in the list of the world's busiest cargo airports in April, latest statistics from the Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI) show.</p>
<p>Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier, Federal Express, remained the world's busiest cargo airport in April 1997, ACI said in its monthly survey of 496 airports.</p>
<p>The world's 30 busiest cargo airports in April 1997, with volume in tonnes and percentage change from April 1996,were:</p>
<p>  1 (1)  Memphis	     178,673   up    26.7 pct</p>
<p>  2 (6)  Hong Kong	   150,452   up    18.3</p>
<p>  3 (2)  Los Angeles	 150,032   up    12.6</p>
<p>  4 (3)  Miami		 149,199   up    13.1</p>
<p>  5 (5)  Tokyo-Narita	142,198   up     9.2</p>
<p>  6 (4)  New York/JFK	132,771   up     0.1</p>
<p>  7 (8)  Seoul		 130,562   up    18.9</p>
<p>  8 (7)  Frankfurt	   122,989   up     0.9</p>
<p>  9 (9)  Louisville	  113,396   up     3.6</p>
<p> 10 (10) Singapore	   111,689   up    17.0</p>
<p> 11 (11) Chicago	     109,832   up     9.5</p>
<p> 12 (12) Anchorage*	  104,591   up    12.0</p>
<p> 13 (13) Amsterdam	    99,066   up     8.2</p>
<p> 14 (14) London Heathrow    96,186   up     5.7</p>
<p> 15 (16) New York-Newark    85,315   up    10.8</p>
<p> 16 (15) Paris  CDG	   84,302   up     6.9</p>
<p> 17 (17) Taipei		 73,455   up    16.1</p>
<p> 18 (18) Atlanta		69,593   up    10.4</p>
<p> 19 (19) Dallas Fort Worth  68,990   up    10.0</p>
<p> 20 (22) Dayton		 65,554   up    13.7</p>
<p> 21.(21) Bangkok		62,469   up     7.9</p>
<p> 22 (20) San Francisco	61,563   up     9.7</p>
<p> 23 (23) Tokyo-Haneda	 55,350   up     7.6</p>
<p> 24 (25) Oakland		55,210   up    18.4</p>
<p> 25 (24) Indianapolis	 52,373   up     8.6</p>
<p> 26 (26) Philadelphia	 48,406   up    19.5</p>
<p> 27 (-)  Toledo		 41,815   up    53.4</p>
<p> 28 (27) Brussels	     41,214   up    10.9</p>
<p> 29 (-)  Honolulu	     40,859   up    29.1</p>
<p> 30 (-)  Manila		 38,616   up    27.2</p>
<p>* includes freight and mail in transit as well as loaded/unloaded.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
